"www.sec.gov (https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1776985/000177698526000054/a991bntx_q22026pressreleas.htm)\nciteturn384view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn381view4\",\"pattern\":\"16,634\"}); Total lines: 1812\nL149: Diluted loss per share was €3.24 for the second quarter of 2026, compared to a diluted loss per share of €1.60. Year-to-date diluted loss per share was €5.34, compared to a diluted loss per share of €3.33.\nL150: \nL151: Adjusted diluted loss per share was €2.22 for the second quarter of 2026, compared to an adjusted diluted loss per share of €1.45. Year-to-date adjusted diluted loss per share was €4.17, compared to adjusted diluted loss per share of €3.23.\nL152: Cash, cash equivalents and security investments as of June 30, 2026, were €16,634.2 million, comprising €9,741.0 million in cash and cash equivalents, €5,035.1 million in current security investments disclosed as financial assets and €1,858.1 million in non-current security investments disclosed as financial assets.\nL153: \nL154: Shares outstanding as of June 30, 2026, were 251,204,366, excluding 7,823,121 shares held in treasury.\nL155: In May 2026, BioNTech entered into a share repurchase program, pursuant to which the Company may purchase American Depositary Shares (“ADSs”), each representing one ordinary share of the Company, in the amount of up to $1.0 billion until and including May 6, 2027. During the second quarter of 2026, 1,693,056 ADSs were repurchased at an average price of $89.50 (€77.85), for total consideration of $151.6 million (€131.8 million).\nL156: “We are revising our full-year 2026 financial guidance in light of recently emerged external developments,” said Ramón Zapata, Chief Financial Officer at BioNTech. “Our capital allocation strategy is delivering results: our financial position is strong, our share repurchase program is well underway, and we continue to make meaningful progress across our pipeline. Moving forward, we continue to execute on our strategy to turn BioNTech into a multi-product biopharmaceutical company by 2030.”\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nwww.sec.gov (https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/796343/000079634326000147/adbeex991q326.htm)\nciteturn384view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn381view5\",\"pattern\":\"5.42\"}); Total lines: 410\nL352: * * *\nL353: \nL354: Reconciliation of GAAP to Non-GAAP Financial Targets and Assumptions (continued)\nL355: \nL356: The following tables show Adobe's updated annual fiscal year 2026 financial targets and assumptions reconciled to non-GAAP financial targets and assumptions included in this release.\nL357:  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\nL358: (Shares in millions)  | Fiscal Year 2026\nL359:  | Low  |  | High\nL360: Diluted net income per share:  |  |  |\nL361:  |  |  |\nL362: GAAP diluted net income per share  | $  | 18.12   |  |  |  | $  | 18.17   |  |\nL363: Stock-based and deferred compensation expense  |  | 5.42   |  |  |  |  | 5.42   |  |\nL364: Amortization of intangibles  |  | 0.51   |  |  |  |  | 0.51   |  |\nL365: Impairment of goodwill  |  | 0.18   |  |  |  |  | 0.18   |  |\nL366: Loss contingency  |  | 0.23   |  |  |  |  | 0.23   |  |\nL367: Acquisition-related expenses  |  | 0.14   |  |  |  |  | 0.14   |  |\nL368: Investment (gains) losses, net  |  | (0.04)  |  |  |  |  | (0.04)  |  |\nL369: Income tax adjustments  |  | (0.11)  |  |  |  |  | (0.11)  |  |\nL370: Non-GAAP diluted net income per share  | $  | 24.45   |  |  |  | $  | 24.50   |  |\nL371:  |  |  |\nL372: Shares used to compute diluted net income per share  | 400   |  |  |  | 400   |  |\nL373:  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\nL374:  | Fiscal Year 2026\nL375: Operating margin:  |\nL376:  |\nL377: GAAP operating margin  |  | 35.0   |  | %\nL378: Stock-based and deferred compensation expense 