lan for a special distribution of $5.00 per share to be paid by the end of August 2026. Upon payment of this special distribution, in total, we will have returned $15.00 per share or $3.4 billion to our shareholders this year while repaying all debt and redeeming all preferred equity.\nL59: We are pleased with the outcome of our divestiture strategy as it has unlocked significant value for our shareholders while positioning the business for future value creation. Following, the special distribution, we expect to end the year with between $700 and $750 million of cash with no outstanding debt allowing us to further invest in Vistance. In addition in 2027, we expect a tax refund of $160 million related to our divesture tax strategy.\nL60: We will have significant funds to evaluate growth opportunities including organic and inorganic investments. These investments could range from investing more aggressively in existing or new technology to evaluating potential acquisitions to broaden the markets we participate in, our technology portfolio and our customer base.\nL61: As part of our investment strategy, we will continue to evaluate stock buybacks under the $100 million of authority the Board has approved for the buyback program” said Chuck Treadway, President and Chief Executive Officer.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nwww.sec.gov (https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1438423/000162828026053376/mram-20260630xexx991.htm)\nciteturn384view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn381view8\",\"pattern\":\"1,374\"}); Total lines: 309\nL279: Stock-Based Compensation, SG&A  | (844)  |  |  |  |  | (821)  |  |  |  |  | (809)  |  |  |  |\nL280: Litigation Costs  | (4,027)  |  |  |  |  | —   |  |  |  |  | (1,629)  |  |  |  |\nL281: Non-recurring Engineering Fees (NRE)  | (1,050)  |  |  |  |  | —   |  |  |  |  | —   |  |  |  |\nL282: Non-GAAP  | $  | 8,187   |  |  | 43.7  | %  |